1. Why is 'Squash and Merge' preferable over standard merge commits for small feature branches in team
projects?

  Squash and merge combines all small commits, especially wip/fix commits into a single commit applied to main, so that it doesn't clusters the history with atomic commits


2. Describe the difference between 'Add single comment' and 'Start a review' on GitHub. Why is batching
important?

  Single comment adds a general feedback/clarification/follow up question without doing any actions like block/approve of the PR. Batching important because it saves time and makes code reviews easier and more efficient.


3. How do Branch Protection Rules prevent accidental production breakage?


It adds extra layers of approvals/review before the code reaches the main production branch, preventing accidents and slips of code into the main without required policy of code review


4. When a remote conflict occurs in a PR, why is it better to merge origin/main into your feature branch
locally rather than forcing a push?


Because you can resolve the conflicts locally instead of forcing a push, making the possibility of accident or breaking a code much lower and with less risks
